# homma-core backlog

Designed and deferred. Names are unbackticked on purpose so the design-doc lint
does not look for them in source.

## The daemon re-running the slow half

The hook runs what a push can wait for. Full feature matrices, coverage and the
publish dry run are the slow half, and the daemon, which is homma's one
background actor, could run them on a new dev tip and append a second record
that the release then prefers. Named so it lands on the daemon rather than on a
second scheduler.

## Per-lint statuses from mockspace

The commit status mechanism generalises: every mockspace lint can post its own
status on the sha it judged, and a ruleset can require any subset of them on
either trunk. That is mockspace's to build and homma's to consume, and the
context name a lint posts under wants deciding once, together.

## A version tag with no forge release

A release whose tag reached the remote and whose forge release never came is
half done, and the check does not say so: the forge client reads repositories
and commits but no releases. A read of the releases on a tag, and a check id
naming each version tag the remote holds with none, finish it; the run's step 7
already takes a release that exists as made, so the repair is a rerun of it.

## The rest of the release check catalogue

The rows the release check does not carry yet, each needing a source it does not
have. A built bundle and the published tarball: reg.hash, reg.filelist,
reg.notrepo, reg.tests.absent, reg.entrypoint, reg.readme, reg.licence,
reg.size and the bld set. A deno manifest's exports and include at each tag:
man.exports, man.exports.exist, man.include.exist, man.include.covers,
man.exclude.sane, man.export.vanished, man.name.*, man.licence.field,
man.description. A forge's pull request listing: branch.pr. The npm side read
against jsr beyond the version sets: both.samename, both.notsquatted,
both.bridge, both.deprecated, both.order, both.latest, both.missing, with
order.npm.*, semver.gaps.npm, semver.prerelease.before, semver.latest,
semver.first, semver.major.zero, order.cascade, order.scars and
reg.yanked.reason. The internal dependency graph: the dep set. The readme's
install lines and banned words: doc.readme.current, doc.readme.install,
doc.readme.works, doc.banned, doc.repo.link. And tag.signed, ref.dangling,
hist.secret.past, hist.lockfile and hist.linear. branch.stale is not owed: a
remote branch carrying nothing the trunk lacks is one branch.merged names.

## A jsr backfill publisher

Publishing every tagged and unpublished jsr version in order, each dry-run in a
worktree of its tag first, with the readme's examples type-checked: a second
publish path beside the release run, for the history a release run never
publishes. It wants the bundle source above, and the release run's own publish
step to share.
